---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How MyGameDNA collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal data."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy"
>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <article class="max-w-none space-y-6 text-(--color-text)">
      <header class="border-b border-(--color-border) pb-6">
        <h1
          class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text) sm:text-4xl"
        >
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 14 September 2026</p>
      </header>

      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        MyGameDNA classifies games across skill dimensions and lets people
        contribute their own ratings and scores. This policy explains what
        personal data we collect, why we collect it, and the choices you have.
        It covers the MyGameDNA website and its questionnaire, catalogue,
        rankings, and profile features.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        If you have a question or a request about your data, contact us at
        alerts@gamedna.my.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        1. Information you provide
      </h2>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Account details</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        When you create an account we store your username, your email address,
        and a hashed password. We never store your password in plain text. You
        may optionally add a first name, a last name, and a short biography. If
        you fill in your top-games list, it is shown on your public profile
        alongside your username, biography, and the classifications you publish.
      </p>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Activity</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We store the answers you submit in the questionnaire and the resulting
        Challenge and Reward classification profiles. We store the game scores
        you submit. If you report another user, we store the report and the
        moderation records that arise from handling it.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        2. Information we collect automatically
      </h2>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Server logs</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Our infrastructure records standard request logs, which include your IP
        address, your browser&rsquo;s user-agent string, and the time of the
        request. We use these logs to operate and secure the service.
      </p>
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Rate limiting</h3>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        To stop automated abuse we keep counters keyed by hashed identifiers
        rather than raw values. The counters exist to throttle requests; they
        are not used to build a profile of you.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        3. Cookies and browser storage
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We use a small number of cookies and browser storage keys.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)"
            >sessionid cookie.</span
          > An HttpOnly cookie that identifies your signed-in session. It is required
          to stay logged in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)">CSRF cookie.</span> A cookie
          that protects forms against cross-site request forgery.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)"
            >sessionStorage auth-status cache.</span
          >
          Remembers whether the interface should show a signed-in or signed-out navbar,
          so the header does not flicker while it re-checks. It is cleared when you
          close the tab.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)"
            >localStorage questionnaire drafts.</span
          >
          Saves questionnaire answers you have not submitted yet so you can resume
          later. Drafts are automatically discarded 7 days after they are written.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        4. Anti-abuse and security
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We use Google reCAPTCHA v3 on signup, login, and administrative actions.
        When it runs, Google receives signals from your browser, such as your
        interaction patterns and device information, and handles them under
        Google&rsquo;s own privacy terms.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Our content delivery network resolves the client IP address of each
        request and forwards it to our backend so that abuse prevention and rate
        limiting work correctly.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        5. Service providers
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We rely on a small set of processors to run the service. They handle
        data only on our instructions:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Neon</span> &mdash; managed
          PostgreSQL database, hosted on AWS in the ap-southeast-1 (Singapore) region.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Render</span> &mdash; hosting
          for the Django backend.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Vercel</span> &mdash; hosting
          for the frontend.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)"
            >Resend, with ZeptoMail as a failover</span
          >
          &mdash; sending outgoing email such as verification and password-reset messages.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Google</span> &mdash; reCAPTCHA.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)"
            >Steam storefront API</span
          >
          &mdash; fetching game metadata. This happens server-side; we do not send
          user data to Valve.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        6. What we do not do
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We do not sell your personal data. We do not use it for advertising or
        to build advertising audiences.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-text)">Analytics.</span> If a Google
        Analytics measurement ID is configured, the production site loads Google Analytics
        (gtag), which sets its own cookies and collects usage measurements. When no
        measurement ID is configured, no analytics script is loaded and no analytics
        request is made.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        7. Retention and deletion
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We keep account and activity data for as long as your account exists.
        You can request deletion of your account; the request starts a workflow
        backed by a scheduled deletion job that removes your account and its
        associated personal data. Some records, such as moderation records and
        security logs, may be retained for a limited period where we need them
        to resolve disputes, enforce our terms, or meet legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        8. Your rights
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct,
        delete, port, or object to our processing of your personal data. To make
        a request, contact us at alerts@gamedna.my. We will respond within the
        time required by applicable law.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        MyGameDNA is operated from Malaysia, and the Malaysian Personal Data
        Protection Act 2010 (PDPA) applies. If you are in the EU or the UK, you
        also have rights in the style of the GDPR, including the right to lodge
        a complaint with your local supervisory authority.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        9. Children
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The service is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect
        personal data from children. If you believe a child has provided us with
        personal data, contact us at alerts@gamedna.my and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        10. International transfers
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Our processors may store and process data outside Malaysia, including in
        Singapore and the United States. Where required, we rely on the
        providers&rsquo; safeguards for cross-border transfers.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        11. Changes to this policy
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        If we make material changes we will update the &ldquo;Last
        updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="border-t border-(--color-border) pt-6 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-(--color-text)"
      >
        12. Contact
      </h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Questions about this policy or your data: alerts@gamedna.my.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
